      "title": "One Exchange, two markets",
      "narration": "The Maryland Health Benefit Exchange is the public corporation created in 2011 that operates Maryland Health Connection. It has two divisions. The Individual Exchange sells qualified health plans to individuals and families and is the only place to receive premium tax credits and cost-sharing reductions; it also screens applicants for Medicaid and the Maryland Children’s Health Program through a single application. The SHOP Exchange, Maryland Health Connection for Small Business, serves small employers with up to 50 employees. Carriers may sell the same plans off the Exchange, but subsidies flow only through it. Rosa shops the Individual Exchange; Priya may use SHOP.",
